WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:06.630
The final season of Game of Thrones is coming,
bringing eight seasons of conflict, politics,

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.559
and mystery to an end.

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:10.679
But how does Game of Thrones begin?

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:15.129
What does the first episode reveal about the
story?

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:20.039
Episode 1 begins with men of the Night’s
Watch attacked by white walkers – an ancient

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:24.890
threat thought to be long dead . We get a
glimpse of a walker’s face – and their

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.590
design changes a lot throughout the series.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:32.390
But they still look very different to the
walkers in the books – who are more ghostly,

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:37.570
and “elegant” . The walkers leave wildling
corpses in a strange shape.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:43.510
And we see the same shape six seasons later,
in carvings made by the children of the forest

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:49.210
. Because the children created the white walkers
, in a ritual with this spiral shape, which

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.450
the walkers also imitate.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:56.620
The walkers copy the symbols of their creators
. But why?

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.070
Maybe it’s a warning.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.170
Cause the walkers don’t kill all these Watchmen
– they seem to let Will go, showing him

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.770
a severed head, then letting him run south.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:10.850
Maybe they want him to warn people that the
walkers are coming.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:15.710
The walkers are intelligent – they have
a deal with Craster where he gives them babies,

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:21.280
to be turned into white walkers . And there
are hints of ancient cooperation between walkers

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.730
and the Night’s Watch.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:25.940
Was there some agreement between humans and
the walkers?

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:29.340
A connection between House Stark and the Night
King?

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:34.000
How might this relate to the Wall, the world’s
irregular seasons, and the legendary hero

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.230
Azor Ahai?

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:39.869
The show’s creators said there are three
“holy shit moments” in Game of Thrones

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:46.700
– the sacrifice of Shireen, the origin of
Hodor, and one more shock at the end . Maybe

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.940
we’ll learn the true nature and motivations
of the white walkers.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:56.590
Also, if you wanna get tinfoil, this symbol
of a line through a circle appears all through

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.590
the series.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:03.010
It kind of looks like this badge the walkers
wear – and if you zoom in some more – well

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.530
it’s probably nothing.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:10.509
In the next scene, we meet the Starks of Winterfell
– the loving parents Catelyn and Ned, the

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:17.360
adventurous Bran, bastard Jon and firstborn
Robb, ladylike Sansa, tomboy Arya, and young

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.360
Rickon.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:24.260
They’re a happy family before all the tragedies
that come – the fall of Bran, death of Ned,

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:30.371
and burning of Winterfell, the Red Wedding,
abuse of Sansa, indoctrination of Arya, death

00:02:30.371 --> 00:02:35.590
of Jon, death of Rickon – this family suffers
so much.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:40.659
And while they can rebuild, they’ll never
get back what they’d once had.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.889
Even now, things aren’t perfect.

00:02:42.889 --> 00:02:49.209
Catelyn resents Jon, because Jon is Ned’s
bastard – a living reminder of her husband’s

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:50.209
infidelity.

00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:53.269
Except now we know that Jon actually isn’t
Ned’s bastard.

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:59.340
Jon is the son of Ned’s sister Lyanna with
Rhaegar Targaryen . Ned says Jon is his to

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:05.510
protect Jon from King Robert, who would kill
Jon if he knew he was Targaryen . So all these

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:11.810
years, Ned lies to his beloved wife Cat, to
keep his promise to Lyanna . You can see the

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:16.349
pain this causes – to him and Cat and Jon.

00:03:16.349 --> 00:03:21.930
There’s also tension with Arya, who doesn’t
fit the gender role she’s expected to play.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:26.260
And Theon Greyjoy is an outsider – as a
ward from the Iron Islands.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:31.280
He stands here with Rodrik, who Theon later
kills when he attacks Winterfell.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.639
Theon, Jon and Arya all feel like they don’t
fit in , and that drives them to find new

00:03:36.639 --> 00:03:41.709
identities – Theon with the Greyjoys, Jon
with the Night’s Watch, and Arya with the

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:43.610
Faceless Men.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.989
The Starks capture Will, the Watchman who
survived the start of the episode.

00:03:47.989 --> 00:03:51.859
He says he saw white walkers , but no one
believes him.

00:03:51.859 --> 00:03:56.809
Maybe if someone listened, and investigated,
this whole story would go differently.

00:03:56.809 --> 00:04:01.700
But the penalty for leaving the Watch is death,
so Will is executed.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.980
Ned kills Will himself, because he believes
that “The man who passes the sentence should

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:11.959
swing the sword” . Robb and Jon later follow
Ned’s example . Even Theon does the same

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:18.049
with Rodrik . Cause Ned represents honour
and justice and personal responsibility.

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:22.960
You can say that these values are what lead
to Ned’s death – but Ned’s legacy lives

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.080
on in House Stark.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.330
Compare Ned to Tywin Lannister.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:32.630
He’s obsessed with family legacy , and his
brutality and treachery make the Lannisters

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:33.789
powerful.

00:04:33.789 --> 00:04:40.100
But after he dies, his house collapses – his
children turn on each other, and all his grandkids

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.100
die.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:46.830
Tywin’s brutal legacy fails, but Ned’s
survives – because he’s a leader who people

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:49.389
truly believe in.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:54.639
After the execution, the Starks find a dead
direwolf and a dead stag – foreshadowing

00:04:54.639 --> 00:04:59.600
the deaths of Ned and Robert, whose sigils
are a direwolf and stag.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:04.919
But the dead direwolf has six pups – one
for each Stark kid.

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:10.060
Direwolves are mystical creatures, symbolising
special destinies for the Starks – especially

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:15.870
Bran, who learns to warg his wolf, and for
Jon, with his albino wolf.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:21.610
So this is about the dying of an older generation,
and the rise of a new generation – like

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.449
the passing of the seasons.

00:05:24.449 --> 00:05:27.870
Down in King’s Landing, we meet Cersei and
Jaime Lannister.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:33.370
Jaime is a careless , arrogant Prince Charming
– so different to the responsible, humbled

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:35.229
Jaime of later seasons.

00:05:35.229 --> 00:05:40.050
But early Cersei’s not so different – she
has all the ambition and resentment that leads

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:44.810
to her tyranny later on – go watch our videos
on Cersei and Jaime for more.

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:50.819
We’re also introduced to Tyrion, the lecherous
Imp . He’s a more lighthearted character

00:05:50.819 --> 00:05:53.080
before all his suffering later on.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:58.510
There’s also much more sex and nudity in
the early seasons of Thrones – Season 7

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:02.270
barely has any , maybe cause of criticism
from the media.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:06.120
We meet the prostitute Ros, who has a long
arc in the show.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:10.689
She moves to King’s Landing, works for Littlefinger
, and Varys , and gives us the perspective

00:06:10.689 --> 00:06:15.920
of a common person among the nobility . Ros
moves up in the world, and climbs her way

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:21.139
out of sex work . But Littlefinger finds out
that she’s spying on him, and gives her

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:27.710
to Joffrey – so Ros becomes another victim
of the Game of Thrones.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:32.340
Back at Winterfell, we’re introduced to
another important character – Jon Snow’s

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.340
abs.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:38.740
These abs go through some complex character
development, too much to cover in this video.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:43.630
King Robert Baratheon arrives, and he greets
each of the Starks differently.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:49.830
He touches Ned, Catelyn, Robb and Rickon – and
all these characters die, while the Starks

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:52.389
he doesn’t touch are still alive.

00:06:52.389 --> 00:06:57.919
Robert asks Arya what her name is – just
like the Faceless Men ask Arya what her name

00:06:57.919 --> 00:07:03.230
is, when she’s trained to be “no one”
. Robert tells Bran he’ll “be a soldier”

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:07.879
. Bran’s injury ends his dream of being
a knight , but you can say he’s now a “soldier”

00:07:07.879 --> 00:07:10.370
in the war against the white walkers.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:16.159
We see Bran climbing, and it’s tragic how
happy he is running and jumping before he’s

00:07:16.159 --> 00:07:22.169
paralysed – and before he loses his personality,
as the emotionless three-eyed raven . While

00:07:22.169 --> 00:07:27.319
climbing, Bran sees the world from above,
just like he later uses ravens to magically

00:07:27.319 --> 00:07:29.250
see the world from above.

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:34.259
His whole power as the three-eyed raven is
to “see” things . And this episode, Bran

00:07:34.259 --> 00:07:40.310
sees a lot – he sees Will get killed , sees
Cersei and Jaime make babies . Bran says he

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.530
sees “the king” “coming” , just like
he later sees the Night King “coming”

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:49.000
. So there’s a lot of foreshadowing happening
this episode.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:54.370
Robert and Ned visit the Winterfell crypts,
and talk about Lyanna – Ned’s sister who

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.469
Robert loved.

00:07:55.469 --> 00:07:58.729
Robert still hates the Targaryens for taking
Lyanna.

00:07:58.729 --> 00:08:03.270
Ned says “The Targaryens are gone”, but
Robert says “Not all of them” . He’s

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:06.039
talking about Daenerys and Viserys Targaryen.

00:08:06.039 --> 00:08:10.310
But this can also refer to Jon, aka Aegon
Targaryen.

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:14.879
So again, Ned is keeping secrets from his
friend Robert.

00:08:14.879 --> 00:08:19.680
Over in the east, we meet the Targaryens – Daenerys
and Viserys.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:24.630
Dany is meek and afraid, worn down by the
abuse of her brother.

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:29.659
Showrunner David Benioff said Dany is “little
more than a slave” this episode . Maybe

00:08:29.659 --> 00:08:35.630
this experience as a slave is what leads Dany
to fight against slavery in later seasons.

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:40.660
Daenerys takes a bath, and her maid warns
that “It's too hot” – but Dany isn’t

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:41.660
hurt.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:46.120
This foreshadows the later reveal that Dany
can’t be burned by fire . In the books,

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:51.630
Dany can be burned – the thing with Drogo’s
pyre is a one-off “miracle” . But either

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:57.610
way, being the Unburnt connects Dany to the
magic of fire and dragons, and perhaps to

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:04.170
her destiny as Azor Ahai – the hero prophesied
to defeat the white walkers . The Targaryens

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.390
are hosted by Illyrio Mopatis.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:11.690
He soon disappears from the show, but in the
books he’s a much bigger character.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:17.200
He and Varys have a complex conspiracy to
put a different Targaryen on the Throne.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:22.690
But the plan now is to use a Dothraki army
to invade Westeros, so Daenerys is married

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:24.400
to Khal Drogo.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:29.770
Illyrio gives Dany dragon eggs – and the
new Targaryen history book reveals where these

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:31.400
eggs may have come from.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:35.550
We’ll cover this in a new video, so subscribe,
and press the bell.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:41.500
Daenerys looks longingly at the sunset, like
Luke Skywalker – a hero dreaming of something

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:45.950
greater in life . But then Drogo rapes her.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:51.421
In the books, the sex is more consentual – Drogo
asks permission, and Dany says “Yes” . She

00:09:51.421 --> 00:09:54.730
gets some agency and control of her life.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:10:00.670
But in the show, her growth from a slave to
a queen is yet to begin.

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:06.340
Back at Winterfell, there’s an extra playing
Jeyne Poole, who has one of the saddest stories

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.340
in the books.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:11.350
Jeyne is Sansa’s friend, and is excited
to come to King’s Landing.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:16.650
But her father is killed by Lannisters, and
Jeyne’s given to Littlefinger – who uses

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:22.660
her in his brothel . Jeyne is then forced
to pretend to be Arya and to marry Ramsay,

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:29.080
who abuses her horrifically . She escapes,
loses part of her nose to frostbite , and

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.690
heads for the Wall.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:35.790
Some speculate she’ll continue to Braavos
and commit suicide at the House of Black and

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.790
White.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:43.540
Sansa’s innocent young friend suffers as
much as anyone in Game of Thrones.

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:48.870
While the Starks host a feast, Jon stays outside
– because “it might insult the royal family

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:55.060
to seat a bastard in their midst” . Ironically,
Jon isn’t a bastard – as a Targaryen,

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:56.450
he’s royalty.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:11:01.200
And Joffrey, in the feast, isn’t actually
royalty – he’s the bastard of Cersei and

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.390
Jaime.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.420
Jon speaks with uncle Benjen, and Jon says
he wants to join the Night’s Watch.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:11.960
But Benjen warns him that’d mean not having
a family, not fathering sons, and that Jon

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:17.330
might care about that “if [he] knew what
it meant” . Some fans speculate that Benjen

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.830
knows that Jon is a Targaryen.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:24.100
Because Jon joining the Watch would mean giving
up his claim to the Throne.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:28.870
Except Jon may’ve got out of his vows by
dying then being reborn .

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:34.520
We get a moment with Catelyn and Sansa, and
see Sansa’s naïve dreams of marrying Joffrey

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:35.790
and being his queen.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:40.780
Sansa’s arc is all about her losing those
illusions.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:44.670
Catelyn is a woman defined by her love for
her children.

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:47.480
And this episode, she starts to lose them.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:52.210
Cersei says a beauty like Sansa “shouldn't
stay hidden” in the north “forever”

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:56.850
. And it scares Cat to see the scheming Cersei
taking her daughter away.

00:11:56.850 --> 00:12:02.840
And rightly so – cause after this episode,
Cat never sees Sansa again.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:07.730
Jon meets Tyrion, who says “Never forget
what you are” – “Wear it like armor”

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:13.271
so it can’t “be used to hurt you” . This
means to be yourself openly and proudly, to

00:12:13.271 --> 00:12:18.610
embrace your identity as a dwarf or a bastard,
so no one can use it against you.

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:23.930
Except, this doesn’t really work for Tyrion
– in Season 4, he’s sentenced to death

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:30.020
largely because people believe his reputation
as a conniving lecherous Imp . Maybe wearing

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.730
your identity like armour doesn’t work.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:38.800
Cat gets a letter from her sister Lysa saying
the Lannisters killed her husband, Jon Arryn

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:45.080
. But in Season 4 we find out it was actually
Lysa who killed Jon, under the orders of Littlefinger

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:51.020
. Littlefinger caused conflict between the
Starks and Lannisters for his own agenda,

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:54.100
bringing war, death and horror on the Starks.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:13:00.260
It’s only in Season 7 that Littlefinger’s
brought to justice for these crimes.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:05.800
Bran sees Cersei and Jaime’s twincest, so
Jaime pushes him from a tower – starting

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:10.160
Bran’s arc as a psychic tree boy, and Jaime’s
long road to redemption.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:14.090
But what’ll happen if Bran and Jaime meet
again?

00:13:14.090 --> 00:13:17.590
Will Jaime make amends for breaking an innocent
boy?

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:21.330
Will Bran even care now that he’s become
the three-eyed raven?

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:26.730
Whatever happens, Bran’s fall from this
tower represents change – the passing of

00:13:26.730 --> 00:13:29.100
the Starks and the return of the Targaryens,
and the end of summer – for “Winter is

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:33.530
coming”.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:39.200
Season 1 Episode 1 introduces the Starks,
Targaryens, Lannisters, and white walkers.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:43.180
These are the same factions left by the final
season.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:48.390
The Baratheons, Tyrells, Martells, and Greyjoys
are all cool, but they mostly just come then

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:51.930
go – they’re not central to the story
like these guys.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:57.500
It looks like the final season of Game of
Thrones will end the same way it began – with

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:02.120
fire, and ice, and incestuous blonde people.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:06.890
Season 8 is coming in April, so now’s a
good time to read the Game of Thrones books.

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:10.850
As well as the main series, there are the
Dunk and Egg prequels, the worldbook, and

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.450
the new Fire and Blood history book.

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:19.710
Audible is offering 3 months of membership
for $6.95 a month, at audible.com/asx.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:24.060
Each month gets you a free audiobook – so
you could get the first three Thrones books,

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:27.910
or all of these spin-off books, for cheaper
than they’d cost on paper.

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:32.490
You can listen in the car, or the gym, or
in a really hot bath.

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:38.410
Sign up at audible.com/asx, or text asx to
500-500.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:39.410
Thanks for watching.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:44.190
Comment below if you want videos on other
early episodes, please like and subscribe,

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:48.810
and thanks to Patrons Debbie Skou, Katherine
Suarez, Elaine Woodling, Anthony Baudinette,

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:52.590
